":52464204,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNDY0MjA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52464204?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8","html_url":"https://github.com/smix8","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-02T13:46:30Z","updated_at":"2026-01-02T13:53:47Z","body":"> Did you try VisibleOnScreenEnabler2D? Put one as child of VideoStreamPlayer and it should have the same effect.\r\n\r\nWorking with extra nodes is not a viable solution because it causes node and tree related issues, especially when running tool scripts for custom video players. The node-forced video playback is flawed in many ways but that is mostly addressed by fixing the script exposed playback functions with https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114515. This PR here is mostly to protect the inexperienced Godot user from running into performance issues by having a more sensible default behavior.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3705356250/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]